# Lazy evaluation: TypeAssert record guard fires only when field is accessed
# Field `unaccessed` has a type guard but is never accessed, so $error doesn't fire.
# This proves that type guards are lazy (proxy contract semantics).
[@[accessed: Int  unaccessed: Int] [accessed: 42  unaccessed: [raise "should not fire"]]]
---
%.accessed
=== out
Int(42)
